  "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$  into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,j-k \\\\  & =1\\,i+1\\,j-k \\\\  & =i+j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of  $f(s)$ at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$  is $i+j-k.$",
